At 22.02 +0200 2000-09-26, Hans Aberg wrote:
[snip]
>However, the fontenc package will then look for the file 8renc.def, and
>there is no such file at CTAN.
>
>Is there anything amiss in LaTeX here?

Good question (the answer to which would probably be found in =
encguide.tex,
if it had not been for the fact that Frank never completed it). fontinst
has been making 8r<family>.fd files at least since v1.5 (1996), but I =
have
never seen a corresponding 8renc.def ...

Anyway, the solution to your problem is to have LaTeX use the T1 and TS1
encoded Zapf Chancery (virtual) fonts instead. Then all the files you =
need
are to be found on CTAN.

Lars Hellstr=F6m

